cchini into quarterinch thick slices. Stack the slices and cut them into quarter-inch wide julienne strips."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Prepare the turnips in the same manner, cutting them into julienne strips."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Cut the carrots in half crosswise. Prepare them as you did the zucchini and turnips."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Put the carrots in a saucepan with water to cover and salt to taste. Bring to the boil and let simmer two minutes."}, {"position": 5, "text": "Add the turnips and let simmer one minute. Drain quickly."}, {"position": 6, "text": "Heat the butter in a heavy skillet and add the zucchini, carrots, turnips, salt, pepper and shallots. Cook, tossing and stirring the vegetables, about two to three minutes. Do not overcook."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 131.1, "protein_g": 2.2, "carbohydrates_g": 12.0, "fat_g": 9.1, "saturated_fat_g": 5.5, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 22.9, "sodium_mg": 476.4, "fiber_g": 3.5, "sugar_g": 6.8, "unsaturated_fat_g": 3.0, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["french"], "diet": [], "course": ["side dish"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["boil", "carrot", "fall", "saute", "zucchini"]}, "images": [], "rating": null, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1981-03-04", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T00:40:31.179902+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
